detail.abstract:
Purpose-This paper examines the determinants of entrepreneurial resilience, with a particular focus on digital environments characterized by technostress creators. Furthermore, it investigates the mediating role of job recovery in the relationship between technostress and resilience. It also seeks to understand the moderating role of the intrapersonal dimension of eudaimonic workplace well-being and work engagement in the relationship between recovery and resilience.&nbsp; 
<div>
 Design/methodology/approach-Using a sample of 281 entrepreneurs from Morocco, this study tests a second-stage moderated mediation model in a two-step process.&nbsp;
</div>
<div>
 Findings-Results show that job recovery is a strong, positive, and statistically significant predictor of resilience, while technostress has a small but significant positive effect on job recovery. However, the full mediation between technostress and resilience was not supported. Findings also suggest that the positive effect of job recovery on resilience is strongest for entrepreneurs with low intrapersonal well-being and becomes weaker for those with high wellbeing. For individuals already rich in this internal resource, the additional benefit gained from job recovery for building resilience is diminished.&nbsp;
</div>
<div>
 Research limitations/implications-These findings contribute to the literature on entrepreneurial resilience by providing an analysis of the mechanisms and conditions that facilitate its development in the digital era, particularly through job recovery.&nbsp;
</div>
<div>
 Practical implications-These results reinforce the need for entrepreneurs to actively engage in job recovery practices in order to be more resilient.&nbsp;
</div>
<div>
 Originality/value-Exploring resilience from a psychological angle is an unexplored issue to date. Investigating it within the context of the digital challenges faced by entrepreneurs and their corresponding recovery processes offers valuable insights into how resilience is developed and sustained.
</div>
